 "rulebook": "FIBA Official Basketball Rules 2024: Art. 2 (court), Art. 3 and the Basketball Equipment appendix (backboard, ring, size-7 ball), Art. 16 (goal), Art. 43 (free throws)",
 "deviations": [
  "Art. 3 (equipment): the hand holds the ball by a grip switched on and off, not by fingers; the ball is released when the grip is switched off.",
  "Basketball Equipment (basket): the ring is rigid (no pressure release) and the net is only drawn: it does not slow the ball. A goal is judged at the ring: the ball's centre down through the ring's plane and on to one ball diameter below it.",
  "Art. 43.2.3: the ball is at your disposal at the start of the episode; there is no referee, no opponent and no rebound: one throw, and touching the ball after the release ends the attempt."
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Shoot a free throw: from behind the free-throw line, throw the basketball in your right hand so that it enters the basket from above.",
  "rules": "The official basket: a rigid ring of 0.45 m inner diameter (0.018 m metal), its top edge 3.05 m above the floor, its centre 0.375 m in front of a backboard 1.8 m wide and 1.05 m high whose lower edge is 2.9 m above the floor. The ball is a size-7 basketball (0.239 m across, 0.62 kg, it keeps 0.85 of its speed in a bounce on the floor); it flies in air (drag and spin lift). It starts gripped in your right hand and is at your disposal at the start. The free-throw line's edge nearest to you is 4.225 m from the point under the ring's centre; the free-throw semi-circle has a radius of 1.8 m round the middle of that edge. You succeed when, after you have let go of the ball, its centre goes down through the ring's plane inside the ring and on down to one ball diameter below it. You fail if you have not let go of the ball within 5.0 s; if, before the ball has touched the ring or entered the basket, any part of you touches the floor on or beyond the free-throw line's near edge or outside the semi-circle; if any part of you touches the ball more than 0.05 s after you let go of it (it cannot be gripped again); if the ball touches the floor before it is through the ring; if the ball's centre comes up through the ring from below; if you fall before the ball is through (a fall: your pelvis lower than 0.35 m above the floor, or any part of you other than your feet on the floor); or after 12 s.",
  "venue": "A FIBA court. You stand inside the free-throw semi-circle facing the basket (+x), your pelvis 0.35 m behind the free-throw line's near edge and on the line through the ring's centre; the point under the ring's centre is 4.225 m beyond that edge. Painted on the floor: the restricted area, the free-throw line and circle, the three-point line, the no-charge semi-circle. The ball is against the end of your right fist. A ball is released when the hand's grip is switched off.",
  "difficulty": "From a hand about a metre above the floor the 0.62 kg ball needs to leave at about 8 m/s on a steep arc to reach a ring 3.05 m high and more than 4 m away, with a margin of a few centimetres in air that slows it, and within five seconds. A straight-arm swing at the shoulder's speed limit gives less than that, and the body only stands by an open-loop stance."
 },
